the city of Toronto Book Award in 2000 and the recipient of the CBC Canadian Literary Award for short fiction in 2001. Her books have been ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.yorku.ca/laps/huma/canadian-writers/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d22\"},\"ref\":\"d22\",\"snippet\":\" ... Henry and Pushcart Prizes, a Guggenheim Fellowship, and was a finalist for the PEN/Faulkner and Los Angeles Times Book Awards.\\n\\nHe founded and edits the acclaimed literary journal, Conjunctions, for which he received the PEN/Nora Magid Award, and has also published several volumes of poetry, including ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.clmp.org/programs-opportunities/firecracker/firecracker-awards-winners-archive/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d23\"},\"ref\":\"d23\",\"snippet\":\" ... Langston Hughes Medal\\n*\\n\\nLiterary awards\\n\\n**Table 1**\\n\\n| Year | Work | Award | Category | Result | Ref |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 2000 | The Intuitionist | PEN/Hemingway Award | — | | |\\n| 2000 | The Intuitionist | Whiting Awards | Fiction | | |\\n| 2001 | John Henry Days | Los Angeles Times Book Prize | Fiction | | |\\n| 2001 | John Henry Days | National Book Critics Circle Award | Fiction | |\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colson_Whitehead\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d4\"},\"ref\":\"d4\",\"snippet\":\" ... Established by Barbara Kingsolver in 2000 and funded entirely by her, it is awarded biennially to the author of a previously unpublished novel of high literary caliber that exemplifies the prize's founding principles.\\n\\nThe PEN/Faulkner Award for Fiction is a national prize which honors the best ... \",\"title\":\"https://americanwritersmuseum.org/literary-links/literary-awards/?srsltid=AfmBOooYIGTV-EUbGd9xDLmBUtcV_Ts9VM7oqhh4K0lfwTLcUoKmITFg\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d24\"},\"ref\":\"d24\",\"snippet\":\" ... The New York Times named it as one of 100 Notable Books for 2019 and designated it as an Editors' Choice. Amazon selected it as one of the year's Best Books for History. It was longlisted for the Cundill History Prize, an international award recognizing the best ... \",\"title\":\"https://succeed2gether.org/2020-authors-fiction-nonfiction/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"d45a92cf103038129e98125113b6f95962604b8f2fc82b7a83577466ff23127b\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"41ea969dd6fa09e5c64b2809330b2d142c08834f10721c0adb2c99a89c45d4dd\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"international literary prize founded 2000s debut book award\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_11772571a1d948ed9261dfcd"},{"content":"Let me think about this puzzle more carefully. The key clues:\n- An award created in the 2000s\n- A book contender for this award, translated into 25+ languages\n- In the 2010s, the year this book was published, another book (released the preceding year) won this award\n- The prize-winning author was born in the city where the first book's author grew up\n\nThe International Booker Prize was reconfigured in 2016. Let me also consider the Jan Michalski Prize (created 2010), the Folio Prize (created 2014), and the Man Booker International Prize. Let me search more specifically.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Jan Michalski Prize winners 2010s literature\", \"Folio Prize winners 2010s\", \"Man Booker International Prize winners 2010s shortlist\"], \"top_k\": 8}","name":"search"},"id":"call_33e52fccacf847abb76b2776","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"book translated into over 25 languages shortlisted international prize 2010s\", \"novel translated 30 languages contender international literary award 2010s\"], \"top_k\": 8}","name":"search"},"id":"call_939e62eff289406d9a4e5cb7","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d25\"},\"ref\":\"d25\",\"snippet\":\" ... Jan Kasprowicz\\n* Jan Kochanowski\\n* Feliks Konarski\\n* Maria Konopnicka\\n* Julian Kornhauser\\n* Urszula Kozioł\\n* Ignacy Krasicki\\n* Zygmunt Krasiński\\n* Andrzej Krzycki\\n* Paweł Kubisz\\n* Jalu Kurek\\n* Stanisław Jerzy Lec\\n* Jan Lechoń\\n* Bolesław Leśmian\\n* Ewa Lipska\\n* Henryka Łazowertówna\\n* Tadeusz Miciński\\n* Adam Mickiewicz\\n* Grazyna Miller, translation\\n* Czesław Miłosz, 1980 Nobel Prize in Literatur\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Polish_people\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d26\"},\"ref\":\"d26\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2024-05-22\\n---\\nOn challenging preconceived notions\\n\\nPrelude\\n\\nJennifer Croft is an author, critic, and translator of Polish, Ukrainian, and Argentine Spanish, and winner of the International Man Booker Prize for her translation of the Nobel Prize-winning Polish novelist Olga Tokarczuk. She lives in Tulsa, Oklahoma, with ... \",\"title\":\"https://thecreativeindependent.com/people/author-and-translator-jennifer-croft-on-challenging-preconceived-notions/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previousl