https://www.cbc.ca/books/30-books-to-celebrate-30-years-of-writers-company-1.5755144\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d9\"},\"ref\":\"d9\",\"snippet\":\" ... Smith/Books in Canada First Novel Award, the U.S. The Lambda Literary Award, and was named a Notable Book by the American Library Association. Selvadurai's second novel Cinnamon Gardens was published in Canada, the U.K, the USA and was translated into 6 languages: Italian, French ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.yorku.ca/laps/huma/canadian-writers/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d53\"},\"ref\":\"d53\",\"snippet\":\" ... the author, most recently, of \\\"A Terrible Country\\\"; Elisabeth Jaquette, a translator and the executive director of the American Literary Translators Association; Katie Kitamura, whose most recent novel, \\\"A Separation,\\\" has been translated into sixteen languages; Idra Novey, the author of \\\"Those Who Knew,\\\" who teaches fiction at ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.newyorker.com/books/page-turner/the-2019-national-book-awards-longlist-translated-literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d54\"},\"ref\":\"d54\",\"snippet\":\" ... s translation of Donoso's final work, which was published in Spanish posthumously in 2007 under the editorship of Julio Ortega, received the prestigious PEN Center USA 2012 Literary Award for Translation.\\n\\nPenguin Classics Series of Borges' Poetry and Essays, Suzanne Jill Levine, General Editor\\n\\nIn 2010, under ... \",\"title\":\"https://translationstudies.complit.ucsb.edu/publications\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d55\"},\"ref\":\"d55\",\"snippet\":\" ... His first novel Oceana Fine won the 1988 Australian/Vogel Literary Award, the 1990 Miles Franklin Award and the 1990 Vance Palmer Prize for Fiction. He has had a handful of short stories published in newspapers and journals, both Australian and international. In 2005 he started Flood Manuscripts ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.goodreads.com/topic/show/22141667-winners-of-the-miles-franklin-literary-award\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"3dce296f8a3610f2a4d0a13a6e2a12ced0bd5460862b6bbb0652773632c07b31\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"628f82c392078c6fe9a938a1f29b80c160be58d0eae6cabd7a7a222b4c3b19b9\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"novel translated 30 languages contender international literary award 2010s\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_939e62eff289406d9a4e5cb7"},{"content":"A very promising lead: Chigozie Obioma's novels \"The Fishermen\" (2015) and \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) were shortlisted for the Booker Prize and translated into 30 languages. Let me check this against the puzzle.\n\nThe Booker Prize was created in 1969, not the 2000s. But wait — the puzzle says \"originally created in the 2000s (the award itself).\" Let me reconsider. The Man Booker International Prize was created in 2005 (in its earlier form). Let me verify the details of Obioma's books and the Man Booker International Prize.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d49\"}","name":"read"},"id":"call_5b0ebfd3d9ca4948bdd3a1b2","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Man Booker International Prize created 2005 founded history\", \"Chigozie Obioma born city grew up biography\", \"An Orchestra of Minorities published 2019 translated languages\"], \"top_k\": 8}","name":"search"},"id":"call_b0df7131c6144b5bb44ee6fb","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d49\",\"document_chars\":17355,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e1\",\"sha256\":\"79767844ce2071fc5dcf3fb0e64d0cade0ba154ef0fc324d0054c1c767e63138\",\"snapshot\":\"90019ca46504785f620ef12f36abae20080c8c3bc7809053339e4beaa4deb2fd\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: ADVISORS\\ndate: 2022-01-01\\n---\\nADVISORS\\n\\nAdvisors\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated for two dozen prizes for fiction. He was named one of Foreign Policy's 100 Leading Global Thinkers in 2015 and served as a judge of the Booker prize in 2021. He is the Helen S. Lanier Distinguished Professor of English and Creative Writing at the University of Georgia, and the program director of the Oxbelly Writers retreat. His third novel, The Road to the Country, was published in 2024.\\n\\nProgram Manager\\n\\nRosie is a production and event manager based in Athens, Greece, with extensive experience in coordinating high-profile film festivals and cultural events. She holds a degree in Communication, Media and Culture from Athens and pursued further studies in Art History in Paris, culminating in a Master's in Culture & Tourism from Université Paris 1 Panthéon-Sorbonne. Her professional experience includes collaborations with cultural organizations and festivals worldwide, including UNESCO in New York, the Rolex Art Festival, Les Rencontres d'Arles Photo Festival among others. Since 2018, she has served as Festival Coordinator and Special Events Manager for the French Film Festival of Greece, and since 2022, she has been the Head of Production for the Athens International Children's Film Festival. Driven by a deep passion for cultural engagement and sustainable tourism, she continually seeks innovative ways to connect communities through the arts. In her free time, she enjoys playing music and gardening.\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationaler Literaturpreis, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated for two dozen prizes for fiction. He was a judge of the Booker prize in 2021. He is the Helen S. Lanier Professor of Creative Writing and English at the University of Georgia, and the program director of the Oxbelly Fiction Writers program. His third novel, The Road to the Country, will be published in 2024.\\n\\nProgram Manager\\n\\nKaterina Papanikolopoulos joined Faliro House in 2022 as Manager of Special Projects – a position that evolved into her role acting as the 2024 Oxbelly Retreat, Fiction Writers Program Manager. Following her graduation from UCLA (Summa Cum Laude, Art History), Papanikolopoulos founded the non-profit Athens Design Forum (ADF), a platform that advocates for overlooked and generative design histories interwoven with global labor and migration pa\"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":3000,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_5b0ebfd3d9ca4948bdd3a1b2"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d5\"},\"ref\":\"d5\",\"snippet\":\" ... The award has been known as the International Booker Prize since the Man Group ended its association with the prizes in 2019.\\n\\nA Russian version of the Booker Prize was created in 1992 called the Booker-Open Russia Literary Prize, also known as the Russian Booker Prize. In ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d56\"},\"ref\":\"d56\",\"snippet\":\" ... They kept the name Booker when they created the new Man Booker International Prize, but dropped it for the Man Asia Literary Prize.\\n\\nIn Australia, we have The Australian/Vogel Award for an unpublished first manuscript: a collaboration between a newspaper and a health foods company. The effect ... \",\"title\":\"https://giramondopublishing.com/heat/archive/beth-driscoll-how-prizes-work-in-the-literary-economy/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d44\"},\"ref\":\"d44\",\"snippet\":\" ... Her work has won the Nobel Prize in Literature, two Scotiabank Giller Prizes, three Governor General's Literary Awards and the Man Booker International Prize. Her first book, Dance of the Happy Shades, was released in 1968, and she continued to write stories until retiring in 2013.\\n\\nWachtel ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/30-books-to-celebrate-30-years-of-writers-company-1.5755144\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d40\"},\"ref\":\"d40\",\"snippet\":\" ... Coetzee | Slow Man | Secker & Warburg | *John Sutherland (chair) *Lindsay Duguid *Rick Gekoski *Josephine Hart *David Sexton |\\n| 2005 The Booker Prizes |url= |access-date=2022-10-19 |website=thebookerprizes.com |language=en |archive-date=10 December 2022 |archive-url= |url-status=live }} | Longlist | Rachel Cusk | In the Fold | Faber ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d43\"},\"ref\":\"d43\",\"snippet\":\" ... Coetzee, Hilary Mantel and Margaret Atwood.Man Booker official site: J. G. Farrell ; Hilary Mantel ; J. M. Coetzee: . Carey won his first Booker Prize in 1988, for Oscar and Lucinda, and won his second Booker Prize in 2001, for True History of the Kelly Gang.John Ezard, \\\"Carey ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Carey_(novelist)\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d3\"},\"ref\":\"d3\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2004\\n\\n- Short-listed for the Booker International Prize, 2005\\n\\n- Banff Centre's National Arts Award, 2005\\n\\n- Edinburgh's International Book Festival Enlightenment Award, 2005\\n\\n- Chicago Tribune Literary Prize, 2005\\n\\n- Markets Initiative Order of the Forest, 2006\\n\\n- Short-listed for Booker International Prize, 2007\\n\\n- Winner Blue Metropolis Literary Grand ... \",\"title\":\"https://margaretatwood.ca/awards-recognitions/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d6\"},\"ref\":\"d6\",\"snippet\":\" ... In such works, Atwood explicitly explores the relation of history and narrative and the processes of creating history.\\n\\nAmong her contributions to Canadian literature, Atwood is a founding trustee of the Griffin Poetry Prize, as well as a founder of the Writers' Trust of Canada, a non-profit ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Atwood\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d57\"},\"ref\":\"d57\",\"snippet\":\" ... The Man Group invested in the prize from 2005 to 2015 renaming it the Man Booker Prize and awarding it every two years. Previously, the Man Booker Prize accepted work from the Commonwealth, Zimbabwe, and Ireland, but from 2014 the international Prize was widened to accept any writing ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.worldatlas.com/articles/the-most-prestigious-literary-awards-in-the-world.html\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"1bf94ad86494e15369ed9e429e9d0eca129200f76549477e354481f70c07d6b4\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"d69f44feeca343509e686ed69e06af6ea74c79892c5fc1838f304084f4a18662\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Man Booker International Prize created 2005 founded history\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d49\"},\"ref\":\"d49\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2022-01-01\\n---\\nADVISORS\\n\\nAdvisors\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d40\"},\"ref\":\"d40\",\"snippet\":\" ... Farrell\\n*Karen Joy Fowler\\n*Linda Grant\\n*Abdulrazak Gurnah\\n*Sarah Hall\\n*Mohsin Hamid\\n*Shirley Hazzard\\n*Philip Hensher\\n*Mary Lawson\\n*David Lodge\\n*Patrick McCabe\\n*Colum McCann\\n*Tom McCarthy\\n*Shena Mackay\\n*Chigozie Obioma